    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d150">

                <pb facs="0245" n="145" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg145"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.00/23713: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Hanna</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-04-26T16:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 26,
                                1920—4 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>123. Your April 24, noon.</p>
                <p>Consul Dawson telegraphed April 22<anchor n="9" xml:id="d150-f1"/> that rebel
                    attack upon Tuxpam April 21 was unsuccessful, but that consular agent has
                    requested protection as situation considered critical. Dawson added that senior
                    American naval officer at Tampico has ordered destroyer <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Thornton</hi> to proceed to Tuxpam.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Colby</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d150-f1" n="9" xml:id="d150-f1-content">
                <p>Telegram not printed.</p>
            </note>
